Feature: Transfer eligible files from Vendor S3 bucket to Purgo S3 folder

  The Databricks PySpark script transfers files from the vendor's S3 bucket to the Purgo S3 folder
  only if:
    - The file is listed in the Vendor S3 folder but not present in either the Purgo S3 folder or the Archive S3 folder.
    - The file is marked as active (active_flag = 'A') in the purgo_playground.ingest_config_master table.
  The script retrieves S3 folder paths from the ingest_config_master table and uses AWS credentials from Databricks secrets.

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks"
    And the Unity Catalog Schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the configuration table is "ingest_config_master"
    And AWS credentials are retrieved from Databricks secret scope "aws_keys" with keys "access_key" and "secret_key"
    And the script retrieves S3 paths from columns "s3_vendor_path", "s3_landing_path", and "s3_archive_path" in "ingest_config_master"
    And only files with "active_flag" = "A" in "ingest_config_master" are eligible for transfer
    And file name matching is case-sensitive and includes file extensions
    And only files in the root of the S3 folders are considered (no recursive search)
    And files are copied (not moved) from Vendor to Purgo S3 folder

  Scenario Outline: Transfer eligible active files from Vendor S3 to Purgo S3
    Given the ingest_config_master table contains a row with
      | file_name         | active_flag | s3_vendor_path         | s3_landing_path         | s3_archive_path         |
      | <file_name>       | <flag>      | <vendor_path>          | <purgo_path>            | <archive_path>          |
    And the Vendor S3 folder at "<vendor_path>" contains the file "<file_name>"
    And the Purgo S3 folder at "<purgo_path>" does not contain the file "<file_name>"
    And the Archive S3 folder at "<archive_path>" does not contain the file "<file_name>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<file_name>" is copied from "<vendor_path>" to "<purgo_path>"
    And the file "<file_name>" remains in "<vendor_path>"
    And the file "<file_name>" does not exist in "<archive_path>"

    Examples:
      | file_name         | flag | vendor_path                  | purgo_path                   | archive_path                 |
      | data_20240601.csv | A    | s3://vendor-bucket/folder/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/   | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/   |
      | report1.txt       | A    | s3://vendor-bucket/folder/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/   | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/   |

  Scenario Outline: Do not transfer inactive files (active_flag != 'A')
    Given the ingest_config_master table contains a row with
      | file_name         | active_flag | s3_vendor_path         | s3_landing_path         | s3_archive_path         |
      | <file_name>       | <flag>      | <vendor_path>          | <purgo_path>            | <archive_path>          |
    And the Vendor S3 folder at "<vendor_path>" contains the file "<file_name>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<file_name>" is not copied to "<purgo_path>"
    And the file "<file_name>" remains in "<vendor_path>"
    And the file "<file_name>" does not exist in "<purgo_path>"

    Examples:
      | file_name         | flag | vendor_path                  | purgo_path                   | archive_path                 |
      | data_20240601.csv | I    | s3://vendor-bucket/folder/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/   | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/   |
      | report1.txt       | N    | s3://vendor-bucket/folder/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/   | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/   |

  Scenario Outline: Do not transfer files already present in Purgo S3 folder
    Given the ingest_config_master table contains a row with
      | file_name         | active_flag | s3_vendor_path         | s3_landing_path         | s3_archive_path         |
      | <file_name>       | A           | <vendor_path>          | <purgo_path>            | <archive_path>          |
    And the Vendor S3 folder at "<vendor_path>" contains the file "<file_name>"
    And the Purgo S3 folder at "<purgo_path>" contains the file "<file_name>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<file_name>" is not copied to "<purgo_path>"
    And the file "<file_name>" remains in "<vendor_path>"

    Examples:
      | file_name         | vendor_path                  | purgo_path                   | archive_path                 |
      | data_20240601.csv | s3://vendor-bucket/folder/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/   | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/   |

  Scenario Outline: Do not transfer files already present in Archive S3 folder
    Given the ingest_config_master table contains a row with
      | file_name         | active_flag | s3_vendor_path         | s3_landing_path         | s3_archive_path         |
      | <file_name>       | A           | <vendor_path>          | <purgo_path>            | <archive_path>          |
    And the Vendor S3 folder at "<vendor_path>" contains the file "<file_name>"
    And the Archive S3 folder at "<archive_path>" contains the file "<file_name>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<file_name>" is not copied to "<purgo_path>"
    And the file "<file_name>" remains in "<vendor_path>"

    Examples:
      | file_name         | vendor_path                  | purgo_path                   | archive_path                 |
      | data_20240601.csv | s3://vendor-bucket/folder/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/   | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/   |

  Scenario Outline: Error when AWS credentials are missing or invalid
    Given the Databricks secret scope "aws_keys" does not contain a valid "<missing_key>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the script fails with error message "Missing or invalid AWS credentials: <missing_key>"

    Examples:
      | missing_key  |
      | access_key   |
      | secret_key   |

  Scenario Outline: Error when S3 path is missing in ingest_config_master
    Given the ingest_config_master table contains a row with
      | file_name         | active_flag | s3_vendor_path         | s3_landing_path         | s3_archive_path         |
      | <file_name>       | A           | <vendor_path>          | <purgo_path>            | <archive_path>          |
    And the value for "<missing_column>" is null or empty
    When the script is executed
    Then the script fails with error message "Missing S3 path in ingest_config_master: <missing_column>"

    Examples:
      | file_name         | vendor_path                | purgo_path                 | archive_path               | missing_column    |
      | data_20240601.csv | s3://vendor-bucket/folder/ |                            | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/ | s3_landing_path   |
      | data_20240601.csv |                            | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/ | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/ | s3_vendor_path    |
      | data_20240601.csv | s3://vendor-bucket/folder/ | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/ |                            | s3_archive_path   |

  Scenario Outline: Error when file transfer fails due to permission issues
    Given the ingest_config_master table contains a row with
      | file_name         | active_flag | s3_vendor_path         | s3_landing_path         | s3_archive_path         |
      | <file_name>       | A           | <vendor_path>          | <purgo_path>            | <archive_path>          |
    And the Vendor S3 folder at "<vendor_path>" contains the file "<file_name>"
    And the script does not have permission to read from "<vendor_path>" or write to "<purgo_path>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the script fails with error message "Permission denied for S3 path: <error_path>"

    Examples:
      | file_name         | vendor_path                  | purgo_path                   | archive_path                 | error_path                  |
      | data_20240601.csv | s3://vendor-bucket/folder/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/   | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/   | s3://vendor-bucket/folder/  |
      | data_20240601.csv | s3://vendor-bucket/folder/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/   | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/  |

  Scenario: Do not transfer files in subfolders (non-recursive)
    Given the ingest_config_master table contains a row with
      | file_name         | active_flag | s3_vendor_path         | s3_landing_path         | s3_archive_path         |
      | data_20240601.csv | A           | s3://vendor-bucket/    | s3://purgo-bucket/      | s3://purgo-bucket/      |
    And the Vendor S3 folder at "s3://vendor-bucket/" contains the file "subfolder/data_20240601.csv"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "subfolder/data_20240601.csv" is not copied to "s3://purgo-bucket/"

  Scenario Outline: File name matching is case-sensitive and includes extension
    Given the ingest_config_master table contains a row with
      | file_name         | active_flag | s3_vendor_path         | s3_landing_path         | s3_archive_path         |
      | <config_file>     | A           | <vendor_path>          | <purgo_path>            | <archive_path>          |
    And the Vendor S3 folder at "<vendor_path>" contains the file "<actual_file>"
    And the Purgo S3 folder at "<purgo_path>" does not contain the file "<actual_file>"
    And the Archive S3 folder at "<archive_path>" does not contain the file "<actual_file>"
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<actual_file>" is <should_be_copied> to "<purgo_path>"

    Examples:
      | config_file         | actual_file         | vendor_path                | purgo_path                 | archive_path               | should_be_copied |
      | data_20240601.csv   | data_20240601.csv   | s3://vendor-bucket/folder/ | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/ | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/ | copied           |
      | data_20240601.csv   | DATA_20240601.csv   | s3://vendor-bucket/folder/ | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/ | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/ | not copied       |
      | data_20240601.csv   | data_20240601.txt   | s3://vendor-bucket/folder/ | s3://purgo-bucket/landing/ | s3://purgo-bucket/archive/ | not copied       |

  Scenario: Log transferred files in s3_file_process_log
    Given the ingest_config_master table contains a row with
      | file_name         | active_flag | s3_vendor_path         | s3_landing_path         | s3_archive_path         |
      | data_20240601.csv | A           | s3://vendor-bucket/    | s3://purgo-bucket/      | s3://purgo-bucket/      |
    And the Vendor S3 folder at "s3://vendor-bucket/" contains the file "data_20240601.csv"
    And the Purgo S3 folder at "s3://purgo-bucket/" does not contain the file "data_20240601.csv"
    And the Archive S3 folder at "s3://purgo-bucket/" does not contain the file "data_20240601.csv"
    When the script is executed
    Then the s3_file_process_log table contains a row with
      | file_name         | s3_vendor_path      | s3_landing_path      | s3_archive_path      | file_status | file_processed_date |
      | data_20240601.csv | s3://vendor-bucket/ | s3://purgo-bucket/   | s3://purgo-bucket/   | SUCCESS     | <current_timestamp> |

  Scenario: Log skipped files in s3_file_process_log with status SKIPPED
    Given the ingest_config_master table contains a row with
      | file_name         | active_flag | s3_vendor_path         | s3_landing_path         | s3_archive_path         |
      | data_20240601.csv | A           | s3://vendor-bucket/    | s3://purgo-bucket/      | s3://purgo-bucket/      |
    And the Vendor S3 folder at "s3://vendor-bucket/" contains the file "data_20240601.csv"
    And the Purgo S3 folder at "s3://purgo-bucket/" contains the file "data_20240601.csv"
    When the script is executed
    Then the s3_file_process_log table contains a row with
      | file_name         | s3_vendor_path      | s3_landing_path      | s3_archive_path      | file_status | file_processed_date |
      | data_20240601.csv | s3://vendor-bucket/ | s3://purgo-bucket/   | s3://purgo-bucket/   | SKIPPED     | <current_timestamp> |

  Scenario: Log failed file transfers in s3_file_process_log with status FAILED
    Given the ingest_config_master table contains a row with
      | file_name         | active_flag | s3_vendor_path         | s3_landing_path         | s3_archive_path         |
      | data_20240601.csv | A           | s3://vendor-bucket/    | s3://purgo-bucket/      | s3://purgo-bucket/      |
    And the Vendor S3 folder at "s3://vendor-bucket/" contains the file "data_20240601.csv"
    And the script does not have permission to write to "s3://purgo-bucket/"
    When the script is executed
    Then the s3_file_process_log table contains a row with
      | file_name         | s3_vendor_path      | s3_landing_path      | s3_archive_path      | file_status | file_processed_date |
      | data_20240601.csv | s3://vendor-bucket/ | s3://purgo-bucket/   | s3://purgo-bucket/   | FAILED      | <current_timestamp> |
